Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `view` was consumed by `.to_list()`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/iter_double_drive.jet:6:10
    |
  6 |     b := view.to_list()
    |          ^^^^
  --> tests/ui/iter_double_drive.jet:5:10
    |
  5 |     a := view.to_list()
    |          ^^^^ `view` moved to `.to_list()` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `view` after the move, or give `.to_list()` a copy with `view.copy()` where it moved.
 Note: `view` is one-pass — materialize it first with `view.to_list()`, or create a fresh source for the second drive
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
